#Scholarship policy

Scholarship awards are based on academic merit, need, and active participation in student life. Eligible students may receive partial or full tuition support, research grants, or housing assistance. The scholarship committee reviews applications twice each academic year. Students must maintain a minimum GPA and complete the required service hours to remain eligible. The policy also grants emergency funding for students experiencing temporary financial hardship. All awards require documentation, advisor approval, and a final review before disbursement. Scholarship awards are based on academic merit, need, and active participation in student life. Eligible students may receive partial or full tuition support, research grants, or housing assistance. The scholarship committee reviews applications twice each academic year. Students must maintain a minimum GPA and complete the required service hours to remain eligible. The policy also grants emergency funding for students experiencing temporary financial hardship. All awards require documentation, advisor approval, and a final review before disbursement. Scholarship awards are based on academic merit, need, and active participation in student life. Eligible students may receive partial or full tuition support, research grants, or housing assistance. The scholarship committee reviews applications twice each academic year. Students must maintain a minimum GPA and complete the required service hours to remain eligible. The policy also grants emergency funding for students experiencing temporary financial hardship. All awards require documentation, advisor approval, and a final review before disbursement. Scholarship awards are based on academic merit, need, and active participation in student life. Eligible students may receive partial or full tuition support, research grants, or housing assistance. The scholarship committee reviews applications twice each academic year. Students must maintain a minimum GPA and complete the 